 in 10 000\\n\\nPick 3: 1 in 1000\\n\\nPick 2: 1 in 100\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What\\u2019s the Biggest Pennsylvania Lottery Win?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"In 2018, a Powerball ticket bought in Manheim, Lancaster County, won a $456.7 million jackpot.  The name of the individual is not known. The prize was claimed by the Emerald Legacy Trust, created by the winner for anonymity.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"When Is the Pennsylvania Lottery Results Draw?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The results of the Pennsylvania Lottery become available as follows:\\n\\n \\n\\nMatch 6: Daily at 6:59 pm\\n\\nCash4Life: Mondays and Thursdays at 9 pm \\n\\nCash 5: Daily at 6:59 pm\\n\\nPick 5, Pick 4, Pick 3, and Pick 2: Daily at 1:35 pm and 6:59 pm\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What Is the Pennsylvania Lottery Second Chance?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Players access Pennsylvania lottery Second Chance through the VIP Players Club. Club members have more opportunities to win from previously\\n\\nnon-winning tickets. You can use the Pennsylvania lottery app to scan tickets to enter them for Second Chance.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do I Have to Pay Tax on Pennsylvania Lottery Winnings?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"For wins over $5,000, Pennsylvania Lottery winners pay a state tax of 3.07% and the standard federal tax of 24%\"}}]}</script>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</section>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t",
